# Entries the ensure script asserts in zapret's exclude list, one per line.
#   +name  keep present and active
#   -name  keep out of the way: an active line gets commented out
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# + duolingo.com, duolingo.cn
#   Alibaba-hosted endpoints (tts-static.duolingo.cn, simg-ssl.duolingo.cn)
#   answer a split ClientHello with a TLS alert or plaintext instead of a
#   handshake, so desync has to skip them.
#
# - cloudfront.net
#   The Duolingo web app's audio CDNs (d1vq87e9lcf771, d2pur3iezf4d1j,
#   d1btvuu4dwu627) need the bypass the ISP SNI filter denies them, so the
#   catch-all that would shield them stays inactive. An older repo copy of the
#   exclude list claims this line is load-bearing because a trailing
#   --hostlist-domains profile names those three hosts; that profile is not in
#   /etc/config/zapret any more, so the catch-all is what carries them now.

+duolingo.com
+duolingo.cn
+stepfun.ai
-cloudfront.net
